   },
   {
    "title": "Complex Behaviors in a Discourse - Leadership",
    "description": "•\tThis NLP project determines the degree of leadership quality shown by a member in a chat room based on its socio-linguistic behavioral indices like Topic Control Measure, Cumulative Disagreement Measure and Task Control Measure.\n•\tTopic control is attempt by a chat participant to impose the topic of conversation, while Task control is an effort by one or more members of group to define group’s goal or steer the group towards goal.\n•\tThe data from chat room was processed using Stanford NLP tool into an XML file, Topic Control indices were processed using NLTK.\n•\tDialogue Act Tagging required for Task Control and Disagreement Measure was done using NPS Chat Corpus, NLTK, Sklearn libraries.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jan 2018 - May 2018"
